# panel 214, lane land-214, 2026-10-14 (its provisional resolution; the
# compiler-engineer's shape x15).
#
# SYMPTOM: `int main;` in a header: the C this compiler writes defines `main`, a
# function, and clang refuses it there; told *internal error* at exit 2.
#
# FIX: R3, as the case beside it (`cli/own_names.hero`, `kept`).

extern "ffi-a-header-defining-main-as-an-object-is-told.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function x15_f() -> i32

function main()
    print(x15_f())
